00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:07.349 align:start position:0%
the agriculture and fisheries council  has secured a political agreement on  fishing opportunities for deep sea  stocks for 2015 and 2016 with the  support from an overwhelming majority of  member states the regulation will be  formally adopted at the next council in  december and into force at the start of  next year  it will ensure the sustainable  management of our fish stocks while  taking into account the  economic effects of our decisions as  well deep sea fish have often long  reproduction cycles so the ministers  were aware of the need to be careful  with quotas for those species the  decision will see a small increase in  overall catches for some stocks but  significant reductions for species close  to collapse  no fishing will be allowed for  vulnerable shark species in an effort to  ensure their protection  on agricultural matters many ministers  express concerns about plans to reduce  the common agricultural policy budget in  2015. they believe that russia's import  ban on some foods has already hit the  sector hard enough  the ministers also discussed measures to  help strengthen policies towards young  farmers to help provide a viable future  for european agriculture
 

